WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.610
Millions of Muslims know
a whole book by heart:

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:06.440
all 114 chapters.

3
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:09.490
Muslims believe it began in a cave in 610,

4
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.640
on one night in Ramadan.

5
00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.460
They believe the angel
Jibril brought it in parts,

6
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:16.850
over about 23 years.

7
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.790
For Muslims, these are
not words about God,

8
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.770
but God's own words.

9
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.660
So how does that change the way
the Qur'an is read and kept?

10
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.750
In this mission, you'll read what the
Qur'an itself says about where its words

11
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:30.920
come from.

12
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:35.350
Then you'll weigh up a debate: does
reciting it matter more than understanding

13
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.180
it?

14
00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:41.270
Your mission: find out how belief in God's
own words shapes the way Muslims treat

15
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.110
the Qur'an.
